  "contract": [
    "Increment unsigned 32-bit sequence on every call, read ticks, then reload sequence; only sequence1 or unsigned tick delta >=10000 proceeds.",
    "Store report tick before channel/provider calls. Clear 48 sample bytes and read E3 for 42 or48 bytes through the IQS port, ignoring status.",
    "Capture model pointer before the read. Skip channels with captured configuration[5+i]==ff; null configuration activates every channel.",
    "Compute active count/min/max and append unsigned channel values while the signed output offset is below152; zero active sets minimum0.",
    "Read log modes live. Each enabled header sink decodes SN afresh, reads captured configuration halfword, and reloads sequence. Geometry is8x3 only for24 channels.",
    "snprintf/vsnprintf use ordinary C variadic entries over the selected Arm AAPCS single-pointer va_list representation, retaining the existing C core and bounded-output worker.",
    "Retained log converts its saved raw argument stream to that typed va_list representation before calling the C wrapper."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Direct audit tests model ticks, channel count, SN decode, read/formatter/log providers. Deeper tests execute actual C formatter core, IQS ports, transport and registry against prepared device callbacks.",
    "The new empty-list output when all channels are masked is defined C behavior. The native unwritten private list bytes are excluded from comparison; fourteen C sink checks per audit pass verify an empty string.",
    "Sample buffers are cleared in both stock and C, so partial reads are compared directly. Formatter-return guard probes are controlled-provider tests; normal channel strings fit within160 bytes.",
    "Formatter comparisons cover ordinary AAPCS outputs, destination/count writes, 32/64-bit stream alignment and sampled binary64 formats. They do not assert private saved-register/frame identity or exhaustive formatting semantics.",
    "Retained logger tests execute actual C body/formatter with cold and warm contexts; crash initialization, stdout, and standard memory operations are modeled. Other existing variadic bridges remain outside this change.",
    "Standard copy/fill are modeled due to the previously recorded Unicorn return/IT-state diagnostic. No firmware memory implementation is changed or physical memory-fault claim made.",
    "The final retained caller was built and tested separately. All earlier-tested audit/formatter/provider objects are hash-identical in the final build.",
    "Cold RW checks do not establish final runtime placement. Global sources-check still fails for pre-existing unlisted G2 resident_rom_thumb_set.S; R1 passes.",
    "No final application link, physical bus timing, full call-chain stack budget or device boot proof; byte identity is not required."
  ],
